title: GhostFrame ESXi Implant Persistence and execInstalledOnly Tampering
id: ca688781-fb85-4659-ad61-42398381bb8b
status: experimental
description: Detects the GhostFrame post-exploitation framework on VMware ESXi hosts (Recorded Future Insikt Group, TAG-218 / Settra overlap). The implant vmhostd-core is dropped at /opt/vmhostd-core, persists by editing /etc/rc.local.d/local.sh, and the operator disables the ESXi firewall and the execInstalledOnly control via esxcli roughly every five seconds. Authored from case analysis - not validated against a live sample.
references:
  - https://www.recordedfuture.com/blog/ghostframe-esxi-implant-settra-ransomware
  - https://www.huntress.com/blog/new-settra-ransomware-variant
  - https://gbhackers.com/new-ghostframe-malware-targets-vmware-esxi-servers/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/11
tags:
  - attack.t1003
  - attack.t1562
  - attack.t1685
  - attack.t1090
  - attack.t1219
  - attack.t1070
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: linux
detection:
  selection_implant_image:
    Image|endswith: '/vmhostd-core'
  selection_implant_cmdline:
    CommandLine|contains: 'vmhostd-core'
  selection_local_sh_persistence:
    CommandLine|contains|all:
      - '/etc/rc.local.d/local.sh'
      - 'vmhostd-core'
  selection_execinstalledonly:
    CommandLine|contains|all:
      - 'esxcli'
      - 'execInstalledOnly'
  selection_firewall_disable:
    CommandLine|contains|all:
      - 'esxcli network firewall set'
      - 'false'
  condition: selection_implant_image or selection_implant_cmdline or selection_local_sh_persistence or selection_execinstalledonly or selection_firewall_disable
falsepositives:
  - Administrators legitimately lowering execInstalledOnly or the ESXi firewall during approved maintenance windows
  - Backup or hardening scripts that rewrite /etc/rc.local.d/local.sh
level: high
